# Supabase CLI local state — added 2026-07-30 (Opus audit finding L10).
# `supabase/.temp/` holds files the CLI writes and rewrites as a side effect of commands
# like `supabase link` and `supabase db query` (e.g. `linked-project.json`). It is local
# machine state, not project source, it is untracked, and Prettier has no business
# reformatting it. This was the one *genuine* format:check failure among the 23 reported —
# every other one was a CRLF-versus-LF false failure, now fixed by `.gitattributes`.
supabase/.temp/

# ADR-TRACEABILITY.md — added 2026-08-12, WJ's decision.
# Prettier 3.9.6 has a reproducible bug: reformatting this file's Gaps register table
# corrupts the entire table (truncated words, dropped punctuation, duplicated markup)
# once any cell grows near the current longest-row size (~6,000+ characters). Confirmed
# on a scratch copy before it reached the committed file. New rows are edited by hand to
# approximate the existing column-padding style; `prettier --check` would otherwise flag
# this file on every future edit. Revisit if the table is restructured or the bug is
# fixed upstream — see the note at the top of that file's "Gaps register" section.
docs/Implementation Plan/ADR-TRACEABILITY.md
